d_at":"2026-10-06T07:31:34.660404+00:00","description":"OBJECTIVE: Create reusable information-surface patterns that replace equal-weight KPI/card walls with deliberate hierarchy while preserving canonical token values.\n\nUSER / PROBLEM: Important dashboards can give materially different indicators equal visual weight and overuse containers, producing generic generated-SaaS composition.\n\nCURRENT-STATE EVIDENCE: Inspect BsCard, BsKpiCard, section components, base styles, token usage and representative Ledger/Shop dashboards. Treat canonical token values as locked unless separately approved.\n\nREFERENCE-PATTERN EVIDENCE: Study metric-summary/dashboard hierarchy in one strong enterprise reference plus one domain product. Extract prioritization, grouping, comparison and drill-through behavior.\n\nBUILDING SUIT ADAPTATION: Prefer typography/spacing/proximity/borders before standalone cards. Add/refine a shared metric summary only where reusable. Keep Gold scarce and reserve stronger elevation for temporary surfaces.","engine_stage":"pending","model_profile":"deep","retry_policy_id":"deep-only","workstream_slug":"shared","verification_plan":["Record reference evidence and why each adopted pattern applies.","Capture rendered before/after examples with realistic values, long labels and narrow layouts.","Verify light/dark and EN/AR hierarchy.","Run shared checks, affected builds/typechecks and git diff --check."],"acceptance_criteria":["Reusable primary-metric summary supports a small set of genuinely important measures without one floating card per value.","Ordinary sections can compose without decorative card wrappers where grouping does not require them.","Canonical Building Suit color/radius/typography-family/elevation token values remain unchanged by default.","Gold and semantic colors retain intentional meanings.","BsCard/BsKpiCard remain available where meaningful."]},"after":{"title":"Professionalize metric hierarchy, sections and surface usage","status":"planned