e equal-weight KPI/card walls with deliberate hierarchy while preserving canonical token values.\n\nUSER / PROBLEM: Important dashboards can give materially different indicators equal visual weight and overuse containers, producing generic generated-SaaS composition.\n\nCURRENT-STATE EVIDENCE: Inspect BsCard, BsKpiCard, section components, base styles, token usage and representative Ledger/Shop dashboards. Treat canonical token values as locked unless separately approved.\n\nREFERENCE-PATTERN EVIDENCE: Study metric-summary/dashboard hierarchy in one strong enterprise reference plus one domain product. Extract prioritization, grouping, comparison and drill-through behavior.\n\nBUILDING SUIT ADAPTATION: Prefer typography/spacing/proximity/borders before standalone cards. Add/refine a shared metric summary only where reusable. Keep Gold scarce and reserve stronger elevation for temporary surfaces.\n\nRead root/scoped AGENTS.md, packages/ui/AGENTS.md, docs/shared/ui-ownership.md and docs/shared/atomic-template-route-inventory.json. All presentation, including product-specific screens, belongs in packages/ui; reusable interaction controllers belong in packages/ux. Suits retain business/data/permission logic, typed content/props and semantic commands. Consume one registered complete page template; do not compose local UI. Preserve Solo catalogue/pricing periods, dashboard navigation, shared tabs/card spans and responsive behavior from PR #248.","engine_stage":"pending","model_profile":"deep","retry_policy_id":"deep-only","workstream_slug":"shared","verification_plan":[{"version":2,"kind":"external_gate","description":"Record reference evidence and why each adopted pattern applies.","required":true,"phase":"pre_publication","blocker":"bs-ui-pro-004-evidence-1-required"},{"version":2,"kind":"external_gate","description":"Capture rendered before/after examples with realistic values, long labels and narrow layouts.","required":true,"phase":"pre_publication","blocker":"bs-ui-p